"Download titles (https://help.audible.com/s/article/download-titles)\nciteturn761view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/download-titles\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 176\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: This page has an error. You might just need to refresh it. [Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'bind')]\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Android Ask A Question Downloads Fire TV iOS+3\nL13: ## Download titles\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 3, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Download titles\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: download-titles\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: You can listen to Audible offline by downloading your audiobooks, podcasts, and Originals to your computer or Audible app. Keep in mind that you can only download titles you've purchased with an Audible credit or a credit card to your computer.\nL29: \nL30: In this article:\nL31:   * 【1†How do I download titles in the app?】\nL32:   * 【2†How do I download podcast episodes in the app?】\nL33:   * 【3†How do I download titles on my Apple Watch?】\nL34:   * 【4†How do I download my Audible audiobooks onto my Fire Tablet?】\nL35:   * 【5†Can I download or stream Audible audiobooks on one of my Fire TV devices?】\nL36:   * 【6†How can I stream or download Audible titles on desktop?】\nL37: ## How do I download titles in the app?\nL38: \nL39: Using the 3-dot More menu:\nL40: \nL41:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL42:   2. Select Library.\nL43:   3. Select All Titles\nL44:   4. Locate the title you want to download.\nL45:   5. Select the 3-dot More menu next to the title.\nL46:   6. Select Download.\nL47: \nL48: Using select and hold:\nL49: \nL50:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL51:   2. Select Library.\nL52:   3. Select All Titles\nL53:   4. Locate the title you want to download.\nL54:   5. Select and hold the title you want to download.\nL55:   6. Select Download.\nL56: Once it's done downloading, you can listen offline.\nL57: \nL58: Notes:\nL59: \nL60:   * Make sure you have a stable Wi-Fi connection and enough extra space on your device before downloading.\nL61:   * If you run into any trouble with finding your titles, 【7†try refreshing your Library】.\nL62:   * There is no bulk download option currently available. Titles can only be downloaded one at a time in the app.\nL63: ## How do I download podcast episodes in the app?\nL64: \nL65: Using the 3-dot More menu:\nL66: \nL67:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL68:   2. Select Library.\nL69:   3. Select Podcasts.\nL70:   4. Select the podcast you want to listen to.\nL71:   5. Locate the episode you want to download.\nL72:   6. Select the 3-dot More menu next to the episode.\nL73:   7. Select Download.\nL74: \nL75: Using select and hold:\nL76:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL77:   2. Select Library.\nL78:   3. Select Podcasts.\nL79:   4. Select the podcast you want to listen to.\nL80:   5. Locate the episode you want to download.\nL81:   6. Select and hold the episode.\nL82:   7. Select Download.\nL83: ## How do I download titles on my Apple Watch?\nL84: \nL85:   1. Pair your Bluetooth headphones to your Apple Watch.\nL86:   2. Open the Audible app on your Apple Watch.\nL87:   3. Select Manage Library.\nL88:   4. Sort by Title to see all titles in your library.\nL89:   5. Go back to the Library.\nL90:   6. Select the title you want to download.\nL91: \nL92: The title will begin streaming immediately and will download in the background for offline listening once complete.\nL93: \nL94: If your title is not downloading when selecting it, you need to enable the downloads:\nL95:   1. Select the title you want to download.\nL96:   2. In the player, select the 3-dot More menu.\nL97:   3. Select Data & storage.\nL98:   4. Select Stream & download to enable the downloads.\nL99: ## How do I download my Audible audiobooks onto my Fire Tablet?\nL100: \nL101: For Fire OS 8 and above\nL102: \nL103:   1. Select the Audible app.\nL104:   2. Select the main menu.\nL105:   3. Select Library.\nL106:   4. Select the cover art of the title to be downloaded (make sure to turn your Wi-Fi on).\nL107:   5. You should see your downloaded title under the Downloaded tab.\nL108: \nL109: Note: Audible does not support devices with FireOS 7 and below versions.\nL110: ## Can I download or stream Audible audiobooks on one of my Fire TV devices?\nL111: \nL112: When you install the Audible app to one of your Fire TV devices, the titles in your Library don't need to be downloaded.\nL113: ## How can I stream or download Audible titles on desktop?\nL114: \nL115: You can listen to the titles in your library by using the Cloud Player from any supported browser. If you have access to a computer running Windows 10 or 11, you can use AudibleSync to download titles and sync them to compatible MP3 players or accessibility devices.\nL116: \nL117: To listen to and download audiobooks on a macOS computer, visit 【8†Listen on your macOS device.】\nL118: \nL119: Notes:\nL120:   * 【9†AudibleSync】 does not support bulk downloads. Titles can only be downloaded individually.\nL121: \nL122: Did this answer your question?\nL123: \nL124: 【10†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL125: \nL126: \nL127: \nL128: 【11†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL129: \nL130:  Back to top\nL131: \nL132: 【12†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL133: \nL134: 【13†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL135: ## Need more assistance?\nL136: \nL137: 【14†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL138: \nL139: \nL140: \nL141: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL142: \nL143: \nL144: \nL145: Worst\nL146: \nL147: 1\nL148: \nL149: 2\nL150: \nL151: 3\nL152: \nL153: 4\nL154: \nL155: 5\nL156: \nL157: 6\nL158: \nL159: 7\nL160: \nL161: Best\nL162: \nL163: \nL164: \nL165: Region\nL166: \nL167: United States\nL168: \nL169: Language\nL170: \nL171: English\nL172: \nL173: Loading\nL174: \nL175: Download titles 【15†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nManage clips & notes (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-clips-bookmarks)\nciteturn761view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-clips-bookmarks\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 260\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Android Ask A Question Clips & bookmarks Cloud Player+4\nL13: ## Manage clips & notes\nL14: \nL15:   * Sep 9, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Manage clips & notes\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: manage-clips-bookmarks\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: You can save, edit, delete, and play specific clips of an audiobook right from the player in your app. Creating clips makes it easy to replay your favorite sections, quotes, or bits of dialogue. They can be as long as 44 seconds and as short as 5 seconds. You can also bookmark certain places you'd like to return to later, from both the app or Cloud Player.\nL29: If you're looking for more information about Cloud Player, including how to use it and common troubleshooting techniques, please refer to 【1†Listen on a browser.】\nL30: \nL31: Notes:\nL32: \nL33:   * Any clip you save in the app will also add a bookmark.\nL34:   * Select Go to Bookmark from the app or 【1†Cloud Player】 will resume playback from that exact position.\nL35:   * You aren't able to add or manage clips from the website—only the app.\nL36: \nL37: In this article:\nL38:   * 【2†Save an audio clip】\nL39:   * 【3†Edit an audio clip】\nL40:   * 【4†Add a note to your clip】\nL41:   * 【5†Delete an audio clip】\nL42:   * 【6†Play a saved audio clip】\nL43:   * 【7†Add a bookmark】\nL44:   * 【8†Add a note to a bookmark】\nL45:   * 【9†Access a saved bookmark】\nL46:   * 【10†Delete a saved bookmark】\nL47: ## Save an audio clip\nL48: \nL49: The Audio Clips feature is exclusively accessible through the Audible app on Android and iOS devices.\nL50: \nL51: In the app\nL52: \nL53:   1. Open the title's player screen.\nL54:   2. Select the +Clip icon to automatically save 30 seconds.\nL55: ## Edit an audio clip\nL56: \nL57: You can edit and access the Audio Clip features through the Audible app.\nL58: \nL59: In the app\nL60: \nL61: From the confirmation banner\nL62: \nL63:   1. Open the title's player screen.\nL64:   2. Select the +Clip icon to automatically save 30 seconds.\nL65:   3. Select Edit on the confirmation banner “Clip Saved.”\nL66:   4. Drag the audio clip handles to set your desired beginning and end point.\nL67: \nL68: From Clips & Notes\nL69:   1. Open the title's player screen.\nL70:   2. Select the Clips & Notes button.\nL71:   3. Find the clip you'd like to edit and select the 3-dot menu.\nL72:   4. Select Edit Clip.\nL73:   5. Drag the audio clip handles to set your desired beginning and end point.\nL74: ## Add a note to your clip\nL75: \nL76: You can add notes to your Audio Clips through the Audible app.\nL77: \nL78: In the app\nL79: \nL80: From the confirmation banner\nL81: \nL82:   1. Open the title's player screen.\nL83:   2. Select the +Clip icon to automatically save 30 seconds.\nL84:   3. Select Edit on the confirmation banner “Clip Saved.”\nL85:   4. Enter your note.\nL86:   5. Select Save.\nL87: \nL88: From Clips & Notes\nL89:   1. Open the title's player screen.\nL90:   2. Select the Clips & Notes button.\nL91:   3. Find the clip you'd like to edit and select the 3-dot menu.\nL92:   4. Select Edit Clip.\nL93:   5. Enter your note.\nL94:   6. Select Save.\nL95: ## Delete an audio clip\nL96: \nL97: You can delete an audio clip through the Audio Clips feature through the Audible app.\nL98: \nL99: In the app\nL100: \nL101:   1. Open the title's player screen.\nL102:   2. Select the Clips & Notes button.\nL103:   3. Find the clip you'd like to delete and select the 3-dot menu.\nL104:   4. Select Delete.\nL105:   5. Confirm by selecting Delete.\nL106: ## Play a saved audio clip\nL107: \nL108: You can play and save audio clips through the Audio Clips feature through the Audible app.\nL109: \nL110: In the app\nL111: \nL112:   1. Open the title's player screen.\nL113:   2. Select the Clips & Notes button.\nL114:   3. Find the clip you'd like to play.\nL115:   4. Select Clip to play only a clip or select Start in Player to start listening again from the clip.\nL116: ## Add a bookmark\nL117: \nL118: You can add and access podcast bookmarks in the Audible app or Cloud Player.\nL119: \nL120: In the app\nL121: \nL122:   1. Open the podcast episode.\nL123:   2. Select +Bookmark.\nL124: \nL125: On Cloud Player\nL126: \nL127:   1. Open a title's player screen.\nL128:   2. Select Add a bookmark.\nL129: ## Add a note to a bookmark\nL130: \nL131: You can add notes to your bookmarks through the Cloud Player and the Audible app.\nL132: \nL133: In the app\nL134: \nL135: From the confirmation banner\nL136: \nL137:   1. Open the podcast episode.\nL138:   2. Select +Bookmark.\nL139:   3. Select Add note on the confirmation banner “Bookmark has been saved.”\nL140:   4. Enter your note.\nL141:   5. Select Save.\nL142: \nL143: From Clips & Notes\nL144:   1. Open the podcast episode.\nL145:   2. Select the Bookmarks & Notes button.\nL146:   3. Select the 3-dots More menu.\nL147:   4. Select Add note.\nL148:   5. Enter your note.\nL149:   6. Select Save.\nL150: \nL151: On Cloud Player\nL152: \nL153: From the confirmation pop-up\nL154: \nL155:   1. Open a title's player screen.\nL156:   2. Select Add a bookmark.\nL157:   3. Select Add note on the pop-up screen.\nL158:   4. Select Save.\nL159: \nL160: From the Bookmarks menu\nL161:   1. Open a title's player screen.\nL162:   2. Select the main menu at the top.\nL163:   3. Select Bookmarks.\nL164:   4. Find the bookmark you want to edit.\nL165:   5. Select the 3-dot More menu.\nL166:   6. Select Add note.\nL167:   7. Select Save.\nL168: ## Access a saved bookmark\nL169: \nL170: Bookmarks can be accessed in Cloud Player and the Audible app for podcasts on both iOS and Android devices.\nL171: \nL172: In the app\nL173: \nL174:   1. Open the podcast episode.\nL175:   2. Select the Bookmarks & Notes button.\nL176:   3. Select your bookmark.\nL177: \nL178: On Cloud Player\nL179: \nL180:   1. Open a title's player screen.\nL181:   2. Select the main menu at the top.\nL182:   3. Select Bookmarks.\nL183:   4. Find the bookmark you want.\nL184:   5. Select Start in Player.\nL185: ## Delete a saved bookmark\nL186: \nL187: Bookmarks can be accessed and deleted in Cloud Player and the Audible app for podcasts on both iOS and Android devices.\nL188: \nL189: In the app\nL190: \nL191:   1. Open the podcast episode.\nL192:   2. Select the Bookmarks & Notes button.\nL193:   3. Select the 3-dot menu on your saved bookmark.\nL194:   4. Select Delete.\nL195:   5. Confirm by selecting Delete.\nL196: \nL197: On Cloud Player\nL198:   1. Open a title's player screen.\nL199:   2. Select the main menu at the top.\nL200:   3. Select Bookmarks.\nL201:   4. Find the bookmark you want to delete.\nL202:   5. Select the 3-dots More menu.\nL203:   6. Select Delete.\nL204:   7. Confirm by selecting Delete.\nL205: \nL206: Did this answer your question?\nL207: \nL208: 【11†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL209: \nL210: \nL211: \nL212: 【12†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL213: \nL214:  Back to top\nL215: \nL216: 【13†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL217: \nL218: 【14†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL219: ## Need more assistance?\nL220: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMissing title issues (https://help.audible.com/s/article/title-is-missing?language=en_US)\nciteturn761view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/title-is-missing?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 197\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Android Ask A Question iOS Library issues+2\nL13: ## Missing title issues\nL14: \nL15:   * Oct 1, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Missing title issues\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: title-is-missing\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: \nL29: \nL30: The content in the included catalog may rotate from time to time. As a result, a title that was previously included with your membership may not be available anymore. Contact 【1†Audible Customer Service team†www.audible.com】 for assistance with your missing titles.\nL31: There are a few reasons why you're not seeing a title or recent purchase in your Library. After completing a purchase, there may be a few seconds where an audiobook does not appear in your Library on the Audible site or in the app. If after waiting for some time, you cannot find a purchase or title in your Library, you can try the following troubleshooting steps.\nL32: \nL33: In this article:\nL34:   * 【2†Refresh your Library】\nL35:   * 【3†Check your marketplace】\nL36:   * 【4†Sign out and sign back in】\nL37:   * 【5†Check your archive】\nL38:   * 【6†Apply new filters】\nL39:   * 【7†Check your purchase history on the Audible site】\nL40:   * 【8†Update your app】\nL41:   * 【9†Check if the title has been shared (Kids Profile users only)】\nL42: ## Refresh your Library\nL43: \nL44: You can refresh your Library by swiping down from the top of the screen until you see the spinning circle. (That means it's refreshing.)\nL45: \nL46: If a swipe-to-refresh doesn't work, you can do a manual refresh:\nL47: \nL48:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL49:   2. Select Profile.\nL50:   3. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL51:   4. Select Library.\nL52:   5. Select Refresh Library.\nL53: Note: If you're not using the most up-to-date Audible app available for your Android or iOS device, new titles won't appear when you attempt to refresh. See the \"Update your app\" section below if refreshing doesn't resolve the issue.\nL54: ## Check your marketplace\nL55: \nL56: You may be signed in to the wrong Audible marketplace. If that's the case, none of your titles will be available to listen to. Sign out and then sign in to the Audible marketplace where you made your purchases.\nL57:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL58:   2. Go to your Profile.\nL59:   3. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL60:   4. Scroll down and select Sign Out twice.\nL61:   5. Select Sign In once and you'll be brought to the welcome screen.\nL62:   6. Select Marketplace at the bottom of the welcome screen to 【10†Audible.com†audible.com】.\nL63:   7. Return to your Library and check to see if your title is now there.\nL64: If your title is not there, it may be that you made your purchase in a different marketplace (for example 【11†Audible.ca†audible.ca】 or 【12†Audible.au†audible.au】). In this case, you will need to verify if you are registered in 【13†another Audible marketplace】.\nL65: ## Sign out and sign back in\nL66: \nL67: You may simply need to sign out and sign back in to your account:\nL68:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL69:   2. Go to your Profile.\nL70:   3. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL71:   4. Scroll down and select Sign Out twice.\nL72:   5. Select Sign In once and you'll be brought to the welcome screen.\nL73:   6. Select Marketplace at the bottom of the welcome screen to 【10†Audible.com†audible.com】.\nL74:   7. Select Sign In and enter your email address and password.\nL75:   8. Return to your Library and check to see if your title is now there.\nL76: \nL77: For more information, see 【14†Can't sign in or out】.\nL78: ## Check your archive\nL79: \nL80: It could be that the title you're looking for has been archived. Follow these steps to remove the title from your archive:\nL81: \nL82:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL83:   2. Select Library.\nL84:   3. Select Lists at the top of the screen.\nL85:   4. Select Hidden.\nL86:   5. Select the title's 3-dot More menu.\nL87:   6. Select Remove from list.\nL88:   7. Return to your Library and check to see if your title is now there.\nL89: ## Apply new filters\nL90: \nL91: Our filters allow you to change the way you view your titles in the app so you can find what you need faster. For example, you can set a filter so that you see only the titles you haven't started yet.\nL92: \nL93:   1. Go to your Library.\nL94:   2. Select All.\nL95:   3. Select All titles.\nL96:   4. Select the sort icon (up and down arrows) to open up a menu of options:\nL97:     1. Recent\nL98:     2. Length\nL99:     3. Title\nL100:     4. Author\nL101:     5. Release date\nL102: ### Use the In your library filter in catalog search\nL103: \nL104: When searching in the Audible app, you can use the In your library filter to narrow search results to titles in your Library only.\nL105: \nL106:   1. Open the Audible app.\nL107: \nL108:   2. Search for the title you are looking for.\nL109: \nL110:   3. Select In your library from the suggestions that appear to find titles you own.\nL111: \nL112: Use this option to find titles that you own and are no longer available in the Audible catalog.\nL113: ## Check your purchase history on the Audible site\nL114: \nL115: You can check your recent purchase by going to your Purchase history on the Audible site within your account.\nL116: \nL117: Your default payment method may not have gone through—or you may have not hit \"Complete purchase\" to finalize the order. You can check to see if this is the case by visiting the Audible site and going to your Purchase history within your account to see if an order was declined. View purchase history to learn step by step how to do this.\nL118: ## Update your app\nL119: \nL120: If you're not using the most up-to-date Audible app available for your Android or iOS device, new titles won't appear when you attempt to refresh.\nL121: \nL122: Note: An update will only display if there's one available to download. If you're using an older device that doesn't support the latest version of the app, you can continue to listen to all of your audiobooks on another compatible device or in the Audible Cloud Player.\nL123: \nL124: Update the iOS app\nL125:   1. Open the App Store.\nL126:   2. Select your profile icon.\nL127:   3. Find the Audible app.\nL128:   4. Select Update.\nL129: \nL130: Note: If you don't see the Audible app, you may need to swipe down to refresh your list of available updates.\nL131: \nL132: Update the Android app\nL133: \nL134:   1. Open the Google Play Store.\nL135:   2. Select your profile icon.\nL136:   3. Select My apps & games.\nL137:   4. Find the Audible app in the Updates pending list.\nL138:   5. Select Update.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLearn about Read & Listen (https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-with-whispersync-for-voice?language=en_US)\nciteturn761view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-with-whispersync-for-voice?language=en_US\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 154\nL0: Loading\nL1: \nL2: Sorry to interrupt\nL3: \nL4: Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style')\nL5: \nL6: 【0†Refresh】\nL7: \nL8: Skip to Main Content\nL9: \nL10: Related topics\nL11: \nL12: Accessibility Android Cloud Player iOS Kindle+2\nL13: ## Learn about Read & Listen\nL14: \nL15:   * Oct 1, 2026\nL16:   * Knowledge\nL17: \nL18: Title\nL19: \nL20: Learn about Read & Listen\nL21: \nL22: URL Name\nL23: \nL24: listen-with-whispersync-for-voice\nL25: \nL26: Answer\nL27: \nL28: Read & Listen is a feature that keeps track of where you are when you switch between the audiobook and Kindle eBook. It was formerly called Whispersync for Voice. If your position isn't syncing, check your app player settings and make sure 【1†sync listening position】 is turned on.\nL29: When you have Read & Listen supported versions of both the audiobook and Kindle eBook, you can access additional features:\nL30: \nL31:   * 【2†Immersion reading】 lets you read and listen at the same time. The text highlights as the narrator reads. You will need both the audiobook and the Kindle eBook to access this feature.\nL32:   * 【3†Page Sync】 lets you switch between reading a print book and listening to the audiobook without losing your place.\nL33: \nL34: In this article:\nL35:   * 【4†Which devices are supported?】\nL36:   * 【5†How do I use Read & Listen?】\nL37:   * 【6†How do I know if a title has Read & Listen?】\nL38:   * 【7†What does the Read & Listen badge mean?】\nL39:   * 【8†How do I switch between reading and listening?】\nL40:   * 【9†Is there a way to manually sync titles?】\nL41:   * 【10†What happens to your Audible title when you return its companion Kindle eBook?】\nL42: ## Which devices are supported?\nL43: \nL44: The following devices support switching between reading and listening:\nL45: \nL46:   * Audible apps (Android, iOS).\nL47:   * Fire Tablet FOS8 and above.\nL48:   * Kindle Ereader devices from 2022 and above.\nL49:   * Kindle Apps (Android, iOS, Fire Tablet, PC).\nL50: \nL51: For more information about Kindle devices, please visit 【11†Kindle Help Center†www.amazon.com】.\nL52: ## How do I use Read & Listen?\nL53: \nL54: To use Read & Listen, you'll need both the audiobook and Kindle eBook in your Audible and Kindle libraries. To learn how to get the Audible audiobook, visit 【12†Buy an audiobook】.\nL55: ## How do I know if a title has Read & Listen?\nL56: \nL57: The product details for a title will say Read & Listen (formerly \"Whispersync for Voice-ready\") if this feature is available. You can also look for the option to add Audible narration on the Kindle eBook page in Amazon.\nL58: If you own an eligible title, you'll see a \"Read & Listen\" badge next to the cover in the Audible app. You'll also be able to use the Read & Listen filter in your Audible app's Library to find titles you already have access to that are Read & Listen ready.\nL59: ## What does the Read & Listen badge mean?\nL60: \nL61: The Read & Listen badge means the title supports position syncing across your devices. When you own both the audiobook and Kindle eBook for a Read & Listen title, you can:\nL62: \nL63:   * Switch between listening on Audible and reading on Kindle without losing your place.\nL64:   * Use Immersion reading to read and listen at the same time in the Audible app.\nL65: \nL66: To learn more about reading and listening at the same time, see 【2†Learn about immersion reading】.\nL67: ## How do I switch between reading and listening?\nL68: \nL69: If you own the Kindle eBook companion for your audiobook, you can easily switch between listening on Audible and reading on Kindle without losing your place.\nL70: \nL71: Notes:\nL72: \nL73:   * On the Audible app, you can read while listening to a title or just listening.\nL74:   * On the Kindle app, you can read and listen, read the eBook, or just listen to audiobooks if you own both formats.\nL75: \nL76: Switch to Listen from your Kindle app\nL77:   1. From your Kindle book, select the 3-dot More menu.\nL78:   2. Select Listen on Audible.\nL79:   3. Confirm you'd like to open the Audible app.\nL80: \nL81: Switch to Read & Listen from your Audible app\nL82: \nL83:   1. While playing a title, use the toggle above the cover image to switch between Listen and Read & Listen.\nL84: \nL85: For more support with the Kindle app, please visit 【13†Kindle Help Center†www.amazon.com】.\nL86: ## Is there a way to manually sync titles?\nL87: \nL88: Yes, you can sync Kindle and Audible. Read & Listen titles will normally sync in your Audible or Kindle app automatically. If it doesn't, you can manually sync your position as long as your device is connected to the internet.\nL89: \nL90:   1. Go to your Profile.\nL91:   2. Select the Settings gear icon.\nL92:   3. Select Player.\nL93:   4. Scroll down and toggle the Sync device position slider off, then on again.\nL94: ## What happens to your Audible title when you return its companion Kindle eBook?\nL95: When you buy an Audible title at a lower price through the Add Narration offer, the audiobook and Kindle eBook are linked. The \"Add Narration\" offer gives you savings when you buy an audiobook along with the matching Kindle eBook. If you later make an eligible return of that Kindle eBook, Audible will automatically give you a refund for the Audible title and remove it from your Library. The refund will be sent back to the payment method you used. You will get a notification when this happens.\nL96: Learn more about returning a Kindle Book order on the 【13†Kindle Help Center†www.amazon.com】.\nL97: \nL98: Note: Since this is a 1-Click purchase on Amazon, you can only purchase the eBook and audiobook together with your credit card.\nL99: \nL100: Did this answer your question?\nL101: \nL102: 【14†Image: Thumbs Up】Like\nL103: \nL104: \nL105: \nL106: 【15†Image: Thumbs Down】Dislike\nL107: \nL108:  Back to top\nL109: \nL110: 【16†Image: Share link】 Share link\nL111: \nL112: 【17†Image: Download PDF】 Download PDF\nL113: ## Need more assistance?\nL114: \nL115: 【18†Contact us†www.audible.com】\nL116: \nL117: \nL118: \nL119: How satisfied were you with our Help Center today?\nL120: \nL121: \nL122: \nL123: Worst\nL124: \nL125: 1\nL126: \nL127: 2\nL128: \nL129: 3\nL130: \nL131: 4\nL132: \nL133: 5\nL134: \nL135: 6\nL136: \nL137: 7\nL138: \nL139: Best\nL140: \nL141: \nL142: \nL143: Region\nL144: \nL145: United States\nL146: \nL147: Language\nL148: \nL149: English\nL150: \nL151: Loading\nL152: \nL153: Learn about Read & Listen 【19†Adobe ID Syncing iFrame†audible.demdex.net】\n"
